From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PrismML <noreply@prismml.ai>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:18:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Prism: local browser keepalive (no about:blank captures
 after idle gaps)

In local mode the inactivity cleanup thread closed a browser session idle for
browser.inactivity_timeout (120 s), and the agent-browser daemon exited on the
same idle timer. The next non-navigation call (browser_vision, browser_console,
...) then silently created a new session whose tab is about:blank: a white
screenshot, location.href "about:blank", unknown refs. A model that thinks for
more than two minutes between browser calls hits this on most calls (in our
game-building runs, 9.8% of screenshots were this white capture). Each new session
also re-sent the Browserbase "running WITHOUT residential proxies" warning.

- Local headless-Chromium sessions are not reaped for inactivity; they live until
  the agent closes (cleanup_browser at close / atexit, orphan reaper). The daemon
  idle timer becomes HERMES_BROWSER_LOCAL_DAEMON_IDLE_S (default 6 h).
  HERMES_BROWSER_LOCAL_KEEPALIVE=0 restores stock behaviour.
- The last navigated URL is remembered. Before snapshot/click/type/scroll/press/
  console/get_images/vision, a lost page (no live session, or the tab on
  about:blank) is re-opened on that URL and the result carries harness_note
  ("HARNESS NOTE: the browser tab was reset to about:blank (a harness issue, not
  your page). Reloaded <url> ..."). Navigating to about:blank (or going back to
  it) is the model's choice and is not undone.
- browser_vision waits for the load event plus two requestAnimationFrame ticks
  (<= 3 s) before it captures.
- No stealth_warning / stealth_features for local Chromium sessions.
---
 tools/browser_tool.py | 154 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 153 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

